From 225c022c52719c086a0a134a07caed228d5587ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WaleWangPW <396218656@qq.com>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 17:15:38 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 13/22] fix(task): gate absent-target release through sealed
 physicaldelete admission

The first Task06 candidate (0fc8f491) routed ReleaseAbsentArchivedResourceTarget
straight to the repository writer, so ActionReleaseAbsent / releaseExecutor were
unreachable from the production service path and the retained anchor could
transition to released without the central admission lock, inventory, or
root-policy gate.

- Service now holds a physicaldelete.Admission (SetPhysicalDeleteAdmission),
  wired from backendapp.provideWorktreeManager so the task service and the
  worktree manager share the same physicaldelete.New instance and lock domain.
- ReleaseAbsentArchivedResourceTarget invokes the sealed ActionReleaseAbsent
  admission BEFORE any terminal repository read/mutation, then validates the
  receipt (Mutated=false, Executor=ExecutorNone, Action=ActionReleaseAbsent,
  matching ResourceKind/ResourceID). Nil admission, denied admission,
  incomplete inventory, locked-out, mutated receipt, wrong executor, and
  wrong action all fail closed with new typed errors before any repo access.
- New admission_test.go uses an admissionOrderSpy and a releaseRepoSpy to
  prove the order (admission first, exactly one repo call) and the fail-closed
  contract (zero repo calls on every deny / unavailable / mutated / wrong-field
  path). The success test asserts the physical_retained / physical_removed /
  released state contract on the receipt.
